From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt Builder <builder@openwrt.org>
Date: Sun, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: mediatek: silence PHY LED pinctrl warning when not
 present

The Airoha AN7581 internal GbE PHY on the Gemtek XG2010G does not
connect the PHY LED controller to panel LEDs (they are driven via GPIO
LEDs).  In that case the optional "gbe-led" pinctrl state is not present
and devm_pinctrl_get_select() returns -ENODEV.  Only log a warning for
real failures, not for the missing state.

---
 drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
@@ -1313,7 +1313,7 @@
 
 	/* Only now setup pinctrl to avoid bogus blinking */
 	pinctrl = devm_pinctrl_get_select(&phydev->mdio.dev, "gbe-led");
-	if (IS_ERR(pinctrl))
+	if (IS_ERR(pinctrl) && PTR_ERR(pinctrl) != -ENODEV)
 		dev_err(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
 			"Failed to setup PHY LED pinctrl\n");
 
@@ -1425,7 +1425,7 @@
 
 	/* Toggle pinctrl to enable PHY LED */
 	pinctrl = devm_pinctrl_get_select(&phydev->mdio.dev, "gbe-led");
-	if (IS_ERR(pinctrl))
+	if (IS_ERR(pinctrl) && PTR_ERR(pinctrl) != -ENODEV)
 		dev_err(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
 			"Failed to setup PHY LED pinctrl\n");
 
